data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"For a row of $G$ rewards, the advantage is the reward minus the row mean, divided by the row's\npopulation standard deviation plus $\\epsilon$. The population variance is the mean of squared\ndeviations, dividing by $G$. A row where all rewards are equal has zero deviations, so the advantages\nare zero and the division by $\\epsilon$ keeps the result finite."},"hints_note":null}

